<section>
  <h2>Too difficult</h2>
  <p>
    Quality jobs ensure economic independence, foster personal achievement, and
    offer the best protection against poverty[...] The commission will improve
    knowledge of the employment situation of women and men with disabilities,
    identify challenges and propose remedies. It will pay particular attention
    to young people with disabilities in their transition from education to
    employment. It will address intra-job mobility on the open labour market and
    in sheltered workshops, through information exchange and mutual learning. It
    will also address the issue of self employment and quality jobs, including
    aspects such as working conditions and career advancement [...]
  </p>
  Source:{' '}
  <a
    target="tweede"
    href="http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:52010DC0636&from=EN">
    European Disability Strategy 2010-2020
  </a>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Easier</h2>
  <p>
    Jobs are important because they protect people from being poor and make sure
    that people can live independently.
  </p>
  <p>The European Union plans to:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>make workplaces more accessible</li>
    <li>support job training</li>
    <li>increase access to jobs for people with disabilities</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Source{' '}
    <a
      target="tweede"
      href="http://www.google.be/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=4&ved=0CDAQFjAD&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.disability.co.uk%2Fsites%2Fdefault%2Ffiles%2Fresources%2Fdisability%2520strategy%2520ETR%2520final.pdf&ei=1GM3VZ6qB8jcaO6ugOAK&usg=AFQjCNHto1wKJhXuQrnzMmtVk6pm8MbD7A&bvm=bv.91071109,d.d2s&cad=rja">
      Easy to read version of European disability strategy (PDF)
    </a>
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Best practices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Think of your audience when writing texts for them</li>
    <li>Avoid jargon</li>
    <li>Keep texts short</li>
    <li>Sufficient text size</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a
      target="tweede"
      href="https://www.canada.ca/en/treasury-board-secretariat/services/government-communications/canada-content-style-guide.html#toc6">
      Canada content style guide
    </a>
  </p>
</section>
